{#
  module/Schoenstatt/view/schoenstatt/persons/search.phtml, ported **and repaired**.

  The .phtml's table is keyed on `$this->entities` while the controller passes `persons`,
  so it has never rendered; and `$form` is passed and never used, so the search box has
  never been drawn either. Both are fixed here — see App\Controller\PersonsController for
  the measurement and docs/strangler.md for the twelve baseline non-matches it accounts
  for.

  What is *not* changed: the create link and its ACL resource, the four column headers,
  the order of the columns, and the empty `<td>` under "Community" — that cell is empty in
  the .phtml too, because the person projection carries no community field. Filling it
  would be a second feature riding along with a bug fix.

  The search box submits to `persons/search` rather than the contact search, and shows no
  "Advanced search" link: the advanced form searches assignments, not people.
#}
{% extends 'layout.html.twig' %}

{% block content %}
{% include 'schoenstatt/_contact-search-bar.html.twig' with {
    'form': form,
    'center_on_page': persons is null or persons|length == 0,
    'action': action,
    'advanced_link': false,
} only %}
{% if is_allowed('route/persons/create') %}
<a href="{{ laminas_path('persons/create') }}">{{ translate('Add person') }}</a>
{% endif %}
{% if persons is not null and persons|length > 0 %}
{% import 'schoenstatt/_entity-format.html.twig' as format %}
<table class="table">
    <thead>
    <tr>
    <th>{{ translate('Name') }}</th>
    <th>{{ translate('Community') }}</th>
    <th>{{ translate('Email') }}</th>
    <th>{{ translate('Cell phone') }}</th>
    </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
    {% for entity in persons %}
<tr>
    <td>{{ format.entity('person', entity) }}</td>
    <td></td>
    <td>{{ entity.email }}</td>
    <td>{{ entity.cellPhone }}</td>
</tr>
    {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
</table>
{% endif %}
{% endblock %}
